                <pb facs="0865" n="858" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg858"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9728: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-28T15:00:00-04:00">August 28, 1937—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>190. Shanghai’s 583, August 27, 6 p.m. In the opinion of the Department this is a
                    point which you might if opportunity affords mention casually and orally to high
                    officials of the Chinese Government as one appearing to warrant serious
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
